# Rate limiting off for internal testing (hard rule)

Operator directive (Phil, 2026-08-19), clarified same day:

> **Always remove rate limiting when performing testing. Allow removal of
> rate limiting for development testing as a first-class capability.**
>
> **The demo environment put on the public internet has rate limiting.
> Doing internal testing and localization testing/development do not have
> rate limiting enabled.**

## The rule

> **Request rate limiting and AC-7-style lockouts are profile-driven.
> Production and public-internet demo come up limited. Internal testing,
> localization testing, and development (`lab-dev` / AppMode dev) come up
> unlimited by default — agents and developers must not hit HTTP 429
> because they forgot a flag. Configuration is `REQUEST_RATE_LIMITING_ENABLED`
> in `pim-app-config` (`default_dev=false`, `default_prod=true`), never an
> environment variable. Startup always logs the active posture. The
> localization client storm is still a product defect to fix; unlimited
> testing does not excuse a request storm in production.**

## Posture table (operator)

| Environment | Rate limiting |
| --- | --- |
| Public internet demo | **Enabled** — internet-exposed |
| Production | **Enabled** |
| Internal testing / localization testing / development | **Disabled by default** |

## When it applies

Any lab e2e, nav crawl, comprehensive QA, localization walk, or internal
development session against AIC Server. Also when adding or changing
rate-limit / AC-7 lockout code.

## Required

1. **Profile defaults** — `REQUEST_RATE_LIMITING_ENABLED`: `default_dev=false`,
   `default_prod=true`. Prefer `COMPLIANCE_PROFILE=lab-dev` on internal
   hosts so unset values resolve unlimited; commercial / cmmc-l2 / prod
   AppMode stay limited.
2. **Loud posture** — startup `tracing` states enabled vs disabled; when
   disabled, also a `runtime-status.json` warning. Never silently unlimited
   on an internet-exposed host.
3. **Wire tests** — crawls and embedded-live e2e assume lab unlimited
   posture (or set the manifest key via configurator / admin API — never
   `$env:`). Lab helper:
   `pim-offline-server/scripts/Set-LabRequestRateLimitingOff.ps1`.
4. **Still fix client storms** — localization heal/report storms remain
   defects; see
   `pim-offline-server/docs/dev/i18n-429-request-storm-rca-20260819.md`.
5. **Loop cost** — a ~2-minute sweep that becomes multi-hour because of
   429 backoff or rebuild cycles is a **defect**. Disable limiting first;
   locale JSON and Vite — never rebuild to verify those; batch crawl then
   fix then re-crawl once.
6. Mirror this rule to `core-assets/.cursor/rules/` in the same change set.

## Forbidden

- Leaving production or public-internet demo unlimited
- Using an environment variable for this switch
  ([`no-environment-variables.mdc`](no-environment-variables.mdc))
- Hand-editing limiter constants per run instead of the manifest key
- Treating 429 during internal testing as acceptable noise rather than
  fixing profile posture and/or the client storm
- Weakening production defaults
  ([`baseline-security-perfect-always.mdc`](baseline-security-perfect-always.mdc))

## Worked violation → fix

**Violation:** Lab crawl trips AC-7 admin-token lockout after missing-key
POSTs; agents invent `$env:DISABLE_RATE_LIMIT=1` or ask to raise thresholds
ad hoc; public demo inherits unlimited from a copied lab settings file.

**Fix:** Lab `COMPLIANCE_PROFILE=lab-dev` + `default_dev=false` so limiting
is off without a flag; production/demo `default_prod=true`; startup log
names the posture; client heal/negative-cache still lands per the 429 RCA.

