## Origin

2026-08-19 — operator hard rule: always remove rate limiting for testing;
first-class capability. Same-day clarification: public-internet demo and
production stay limited; internal testing / localization / development
are unlimited by default (profile-driven).

Same-day operator rationale (loop cost): **rate limiting on development
and testing systems is a counter-pattern to getting an RC out the door.**
A ~two-minute nav / localization sweep degraded to ~eight hours (~240×)
because agents slept, backed off, and rebuilt around 429s instead of
turning limiting off for the lab profile. The iteration loop is a
first-class deliverable: disable limiting first, then sweep at full
speed; never absorb a slow loop by skipping verification.
